        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಖುಲಾಸೆ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಖುಲಾಸೆ — khulāse — \"an acquittal\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೊನೆಗೆ ನ್ಯಾಯಾಲಯದಿಂದ ಅವನಿಗೆ ಖುಲಾಸೆ ಸಿಕ್ಕಿತು. konege nyāyālayadinda avanige khulāse sikkitu. In the end he was acquitted by the court."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಖುಲಾಸೆ (khulāse) ಆಗು, to be acquitted: ಆರೋಪಿ ಖುಲಾಸೆ (khulāse) ಆದನು."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಖುಲಾಸೆ (khulāse) came into Kannada through Hindustani and is usually traced to Arabic; the exact Arabic source word is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
