            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಳಂಕ — kaḷaṅka — \"a stain; a disgrace\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆ ಮೋಸ ಅವರ ಹೆಸರಿಗೆ ಕಳಂಕ ತಂದಿತು. ā mōsa avara hesarige kaḷaṅka tanditu. That fraud brought a stain on his name."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A stain on a name or a family: ಕಳಂಕ (kaḷaṅka) ತರು."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಳಂಕ (kaḷaṅka) is borrowed from Sanskrit kalaṅka, \"a stain, a spot\" (CDIAL 2911), and also \"defamation\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
