          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆಣೆ — āṇe — \"an oath; a vow\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಾನು ಸತ್ಯ ಹೇಳುತ್ತೇನೆ ಅಂತ ಅವನು ಆಣೆ ಮಾಡಿದನು. nānu satya hēḷuttēne anta avanu āṇe māḍidanu. He swore an oath that he would tell the truth."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆಣೆ (āṇe) ಮಾಡು or ಆಣೆ (āṇe) ಇಡು, to swear. ಆಣೆ (āṇe) is also an old coin, a sixteenth of a rupee."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆಣೆ (āṇe) is usually traced to Sanskrit ājñā, \"a command\" (CDIAL 1095), through a Prakrit form āṇā."
            }
          ]
