          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಗೋಳಾಡು — gōḷāḍu — \"to wail; to lament\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮನೆ ಕಳೆದುಕೊಂಡ ಹೆಂಗಸು ಗೋಳಾಡಿದಳು. mane kaḷedukoṇḍa heṅgasu gōḷāḍidaḷu. The woman who had lost her house wailed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಗೋಳಾಡಿದೆ, gōḷāḍide."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಗೋಳು, wailing, and ಆಡು: to keep on wailing. ಗೋಳು ಹೊಯ್ದುಕೊ is the same."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಗೋಳಾಡು (gōḷāḍu) is a native Dravidian compound: gōḷ, \"the sound of howling, lamenting, wailing\" (DEDR 2252), and āḍu, \"to move, to act\" (DEDR 347)."
            }
          ]
        },
